{"name":"Passion Fruit","hex":"#907895","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"passion fruit","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant, passiflora, that produces an edible fruit.","The edible fruit of the passionflower, Passiflora edulis; a round fruit with a purple or yellow skin which is native to Brazil."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passion_fruit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Passion fruit (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"The passion fruit and granadilla is the fruit of several plants in the genus Passiflora. It is native to subtropical regions of South America from southern Brazil through Paraguay to northern Argentina. The fruit is eaten for its pulp and seeds, and as a juice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Passion_fruits_-_whole_and_halved.jpg/330px-Passion_fruits_-_whole_and_halved.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passion_fruit_(fruit)","wikidata":"Q2224510"},{"title":"Passion Fruit (group)","blocks":[{"text":"Passion Fruit was a German-Dutch Eurodance trio. The first-generation line-up was formed with Blade, Dawn, Pearl, and MC Steve. The second generation was formed with Dutch singers Nathalie van het Ende and Debby St. Maarten and German singer María Serrano Serrano. The lyrics for their songs are a combination of English and Spanish. They were managed by Georg Bergheim. The lead vocalists for the group were Leticia Spormann and Kenneth Clemmons."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passion_Fruit_(group)","wikidata":"Q1968481"},{"title":"Passiflora edulis","blocks":[{"text":"Passiflora edulis, commonly known as passion fruit, is a vine species of passion flower native to southern Brazil, through Paraguay, and northern Argentina. The fruit is a pepo, a type of botanical berry, round to oval, either yellow or dark purple at maturity, with a soft to firm, juicy interior filled with numerous seeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Passiflora_edulis_forma_flavicarpa.jpg/330px-Passiflora_edulis_forma_flavicarpa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passiflora_edulis","wikidata":"Q156790"},{"title":"Fruit","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a fruit is the seed-bearing structure in flowering plants (angiosperms) that is formed from the ovary after flowering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg/330px-Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit","wikidata":"Q3314483"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Funchal_Public_Market_-_16.jpg/500px-Funchal_Public_Market_-_16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Funchal_Public_Market_-_16.jpg/1280px-Funchal_Public_Market_-_16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Funchal_Public_Market_-_16.jpg/500px-Funchal_Public_Market_-_16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A variety of passion fruits at a market in Portugal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFunchal_Public_Market_-_16.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Passionfruit_and_cross_section.jpg/500px-Passionfruit_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Passionfruit_and_cross_section.jpg/1280px-Passionfruit_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Passi